# The cat062 module: values of ASTERIX Category 062 (System Track Data) as the
# category holds them. Used by the pack `asterix-cat062`. Each status bit has a
# raw key here; where `track` has a flag of the same meaning the pack binds
# both to the bit.
#
# The derive lines fill what another format's track does not hold as CAT062
# wants it: the time of day from the instant, the track number from an
# identifier that is a decimal number, and SIM from the three flags of `track`
# that each say the data is not live.
module        cat062
version       0.2.0
distribution  public
source        "EUROCONTROL-SPEC-0149-9, Specification for Surveillance Data Exchange ASTERIX Part 9 Category 062, SDPS Track Messages, Edition 1.21, 5 June 2025, https://www.eurocontrol.int/sites/default/files/2025-06/asterix-cat062-system-track-data-p9-ed1-21.pdf"
uses          track
key  sac            int    -  "I062/010 System Area Code, 0 to 255"
key  sic            int    -  "I062/010 System Identification Code, 0 to 255"
key  time_of_day_s  float  s  "I062/070 Time Of Track Information: seconds since the last UTC midnight, in steps of 1/128 s"
key  track_number   int    -  "I062/040 Track Number, 0 to 65535"
key  mon            int    -  "I062/080 MON: 0 = multisensor track, 1 = monosensor track"
key  cnf            int    -  "I062/080 CNF: 0 = confirmed track, 1 = tentative track"
key  sim            int    -  "I062/080 SIM: 0 = actual track, 1 = simulated track"
key  tse            int    -  "I062/080 TSE: 1 = last message transmitted to the user for the track"
key  cst            int    -  "I062/080 CST: 1 = age of the last received track update is higher than the system dependent threshold (coasting)"
derive  cat062.time_of_day_s  day_seconds  time_ms
derive  cat062.track_number   parse_int    uid
derive  cat062.sim            any          track.simulated  track.header_simulated  track.test_data
